🌊 Oceanus ROV – Python Control & Surface Systems
📌 Overview

This module contains all high-level control, visualization, and AI components of the Oceanus ROV system.

It is responsible for:

🎮 Manual control via joystick
📡 Serial communication with the ROV
🖥️ Surface station GUI (multi-camera monitoring)
📊 Float data acquisition & graphing
🦀 Computer vision (crab detection using YOLO)
🧠 Modules
🎮 1. Joystick Control (control.py)
Functionality
Reads controller input using pygame
Auto-detects FT232 serial ports
Sends real-time commands to two Arduinos
Receives telemetry data (IMU, voltage, leak)
Communication Protocol

Outgoing packet:

ARM RL1 0 ESCUP1 ESCFB1 # FORK RL2 0 ESCUP2 ESCFB2
Key Concepts
Deadzone filtering for joystick stability
PWM mapping (1000–2000 µs for ESCs)
Dual-channel communication (two serial ports)

🖥️ 2. Surface Station GUI (Station_GUI.py)

Functionality

Supports full-screen camera view
Provides:
🛡 Safety button (emergency stop)

🚀 Float task trigger
Technologies
PyQt6 (UI framework)
OpenCV (camera streaming)
Notes
Serial communication is optional (GUI still runs without Arduino)
Depth display is currently simulated

📈 3. Float Data Graphing (float_graph.py)
Functionality
Connects to float Arduino via Bluetooth
Sends command 'S'
Receives logged depth data
Plots depth vs time
Data Format
DATA START
time,depth
...
DATA END
Output
Matplotlib graph
Inverted Y-axis (depth increases downward)
🦀 4. Crab Detection (crab_detector.py)
Functionality
Uses YOLOv8 (Ultralytics)
Detects and counts green crabs
Displays annotated image
Detection Logic
Class ID = 0 → Green crab
Confidence threshold = 0.5
